After the within-benchmark Holm correction, all benchmark--run tests comparing our system with \condNoGoals\ or \condFixedOrder\ remain above the corrected significance threshold.
An exploratory prompt-level summary defined after the main results places our system slightly ahead of both ablations, at \ClusteredFullFixedOrderRate\ [\ClusteredFullFixedOrderInterval], $p=\ClusteredFullFixedOrderP$, against \condFixedOrder\ and \ClusteredFullNoGoalsRate\ [\ClusteredFullNoGoalsInterval], $p=\ClusteredFullNoGoalsP$, against \condNoGoals; the two intervals overlap, so the summary does not rank the components.
The ablations nonetheless keep the full system's advantage over the alternatives: of \PairedSeparationMeasureCount\ paired native and pointwise contrasts with them on WritingBench and HelloBench, intervals exclude zero for \PairedSeparatedNoGoals\ with \condNoGoals\ and \PairedSeparatedFixedOrder\ with \condFixedOrder, against \PairedSeparatedFull\ with our system.\footnote{See Appendix~\ref{app:paired-quality} for these paired differences.}

